// f32 `atan2`, ported from LLVM libc into `core::libm`, against LLVM libc itself. For each pair
// (y, x), given by their bits, this prints the bits of `y.atan2(x)` (a NaN as 2143289344), then
// a hash of 2^20 random pairs. The expected line is what LLVM libc at f475f085bf7b prints, built
// with FMA. The pairs are: five found by searching 8 billion pairs for inputs whose fast result
// is wrong, so that the accurate pass decides them, with all four sign combinations; every pair
// of zeros, ones, infinities, a NaN, subnormals and the largest float; and 300 random pairs.
// The port also matched LLVM libc on 2^30 random pairs.
//
